// Pixel painting on the DualPanto: an 8 × 8 canvas you paint with both handles.
//
// Me is the brush, It is the reader. Move It with your other hand: every cell it
// enters says its colour (a tick means empty). Bring Me onto the same cell as It to
// put the pen down, then move both together to paint. Pull them apart to lift the pen.
//
// Voice commands (say them any time):
//   "red", "green", "blue"   choose the colour and paint
//   "erase"                  remove colour instead
//   "which colour"           says the current colour or mode
//
// Three independent levels; switch with "level one", "level two", "level three":
//   1 Canvas        8 × 8 cells
//   2 Trace         like 1, plus "show red": It moves through all red cells
//   3 Fine canvas   like 1 with 16 × 16 smaller cells
//
// The commands use voice.intent, so other wordings like "make it blue" work too. The
// first run downloads the small on-device model (about 24 MB) and caches it.

void voice.prepareIntents();

voice.command("level {n:number}", ({ n }) => {
  const name = panto.levels[n - 1];
  if (!name) return speak(`There are ${panto.levels.length} levels.`, { interrupt: true });
  panto.loadLevel(name);
});

